WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:05.610
Even though it's been almost 15 years since
the show premiered, NCIS still has a slot

00:00:05.610 --> 00:00:08.250
on our TV screens every Tuesday night.

00:00:08.250 --> 00:00:12.360
Some faces have come and gone over the years,
while others have remained the same since

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:13.360
day one.

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:17.780
But they all have one thing in common: this
was the show that truly brought them into

00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:18.780
the spotlight.

00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:24.520
Here's what the cast of NCIS was up to before
they got the roles that changed their lives.

00:00:24.520 --> 00:00:26.410
Mark Harmon

00:00:26.410 --> 00:00:32.050
Thomas Mark Harmon grew up in Burbank, California,
the youngest of three children to former Heisman-winning

00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:36.010
football player Tom Harmon and actress Elyse
Knox.

00:00:36.010 --> 00:00:39.610
Football was his early passion, but the acting
bug eventually hit.

00:00:39.610 --> 00:00:43.870
Harmon has compiled a fairly impressive filmography
in film and television.

00:00:43.870 --> 00:00:49.390
He's spent a good deal of the last 13 years
as, essentially, the face of NCIS, anchoring

00:00:49.390 --> 00:00:54.219
the show's cast as steely-eyed special agent
Leroy Gibbs since 2003.

00:00:54.219 --> 00:00:58.640
Harmon has starred in more than 300 episodes
of the series since its inception.

00:00:58.640 --> 00:01:00.190
Pauley Perrette

00:01:00.190 --> 00:01:05.610
Pauley Perrette was born in New Orleans, where
she dreamed of one day being a rock star.

00:01:05.610 --> 00:01:10.229
She also entertained the idea of getting into
law enforcement, and went to college for criminal

00:01:10.229 --> 00:01:11.229
science.

00:01:11.229 --> 00:01:13.799
"I thought I was going to be a cop."

00:01:13.799 --> 00:01:17.490
She finally did get the chance to become a
cop — of sorts.

00:01:17.490 --> 00:01:22.029
And she got to entertain millions of NCIS
viewers as Abby Sciuto in the process.

00:01:22.029 --> 00:01:26.599
Perrette was actually introduced into the
NCIS universe during the last two episodes

00:01:26.599 --> 00:01:31.030
of JAG, the Navy-focused show that preceded
NCIS.

00:01:31.030 --> 00:01:32.789
Michael Weatherly

00:01:32.789 --> 00:01:37.499
Born in New York City, Michael Weatherly was
a professional actor for over a decade before

00:01:37.499 --> 00:01:41.359
landing the role of Anthony "Tony" DiNozzo
in NCIS.

00:01:41.359 --> 00:01:46.009
Prior to his breakout role, Weatherly built
a solid career with a variety of memorable

00:01:46.009 --> 00:01:51.959
supporting roles, including Dark Angel, starring
Jessica Alba, to whom he was engaged in 2001.

00:01:51.959 --> 00:01:56.840
Weatherly has spent the intervening years
consistently acting on NCIS and more recently

00:01:56.840 --> 00:01:59.579
with the title role on CBS's Bull.

00:01:59.579 --> 00:02:04.499
His relationship with Alba dissolved in 2003,
but six years later, Weatherly married his

00:02:04.499 --> 00:02:09.989
second wife, an internist named Bojana Janković,
with whom he has two children.

00:02:09.989 --> 00:02:11.980
David McCallum

00:02:11.980 --> 00:02:17.819
Born in 1933 in Glasgow, Scotland, David McCallum
grew up on a diet of classical music courtesy

00:02:17.819 --> 00:02:21.799
of his parents, who encouraged him to pursue
the musical arts himself.

00:02:21.799 --> 00:02:23.829
"Hey, you're good."

00:02:23.829 --> 00:02:25.180
"Of course."

00:02:25.180 --> 00:02:27.790
At first, acting was only a hobby for McCallum.

00:02:27.790 --> 00:02:32.730
He got a job at an opera house as an assistant
manager, performed vocal work on the radio,

00:02:32.730 --> 00:02:35.680
and finally broke into films in 1957.

00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:37.260
He hasn't stopped since.

00:02:37.260 --> 00:02:42.319
That's over 60 years in the industry, which
may explain why he wears his role as NCIS'

00:02:42.319 --> 00:02:44.791
Ducky Mallard as easily as a glove.

00:02:44.791 --> 00:02:49.030
It also doesn't hurt that McCallum followed
around real-life coroners to prepare for his

00:02:49.030 --> 00:02:52.090
role as a medical examiner on the show.

00:02:52.090 --> 00:02:53.090
Sean Murray

00:02:53.090 --> 00:02:56.709
Sean Murray started his acting career early.

00:02:56.709 --> 00:03:02.359
His first break came in the form of a starring
role in the 1993 Disney classic Hocus Pocus.

00:03:02.359 --> 00:03:06.730
But since he's long since lost the vintage
'90s locks, he definitely hasn't lost the

00:03:06.730 --> 00:03:10.670
deadpan charm that made him a breakout star
on NCIS.

00:03:10.670 --> 00:03:15.849
Like Pauley Perrette, he also has a connection
to NCIS predecessor JAG, although Murray played

00:03:15.849 --> 00:03:20.870
an entirely different character from his NCIS
role of Timothy McGee.

00:03:20.870 --> 00:03:22.749
Brian Dietzen

00:03:22.749 --> 00:03:27.450
As a younger man, Brian Dietzen had dreams
of Hollywood success, and the 2003 musical

00:03:27.450 --> 00:03:32.049
comedy From Justin to Kelly gave Dietzen the
chance to step onto the big screen.

00:03:32.049 --> 00:03:36.810
Unfortunately, From Justin to Kelly is...one
of the worst movies ever made.

00:03:36.810 --> 00:03:41.709
But Dietzen managed to beat the odds and joined
the main cast of NCIS the following year.

00:03:41.709 --> 00:03:45.930
Dietzen has now spent more than a decade in
the role of Jimmy Palmer, and although he's

00:03:45.930 --> 00:03:51.050
also appeared in a handful of films, NCIS
is still his most successful and long-running

00:03:51.050 --> 00:03:52.420
gig.

00:03:52.420 --> 00:03:54.029
Rocky Carroll

00:03:54.029 --> 00:03:58.790
Rocky started out acting on the stage at the
Cincinnati School for Creative and Performing

00:03:58.790 --> 00:04:03.189
Arts, the first of two dramatic schools Carroll
attended before moving to New York.

00:04:03.189 --> 00:04:07.439
Carroll remains an actor with great credibility
on Broadway as well as in the popcorn-movie

00:04:07.439 --> 00:04:11.909
world of Hollywood, with an abiding love of
Shakespeare that he's held since youth.

00:04:11.909 --> 00:04:16.799
His character on NCIS, director Leon Vance,
has appeared in all three iterations of the

00:04:16.799 --> 00:04:20.489
series, including Los Angeles and New Orleans.

00:04:20.489 --> 00:04:22.099
Lauren Holly

00:04:22.099 --> 00:04:26.419
Raised in New York, Lauren Holly practiced
cheerleading and studied English before getting

00:04:26.419 --> 00:04:28.610
a start in acting at the age of 20.

00:04:28.610 --> 00:04:33.090
She landed breakout roles on All My Children,
Picket Fences, and Dumb &amp; Dumber.

00:04:33.090 --> 00:04:34.960
"So where you headed?"

00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:36.260
“Aspen.”

00:04:36.260 --> 00:04:38.660
"Hmm, California.

00:04:38.660 --> 00:04:40.040
Beautiful."

00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:47.660
Holly joined the cast of NCIS in 2005 and
became a series regular until 2008, with additional

00:04:47.669 --> 00:04:50.910
appearances in 2012 and 2015.

00:04:50.910 --> 00:04:54.960
Holly now lives in Toronto with her three
sons and has continued working steadily since

00:04:54.960 --> 00:04:57.190
leaving NCIS.

00:04:57.190 --> 00:04:59.389
Emily Wickersham

00:04:59.389 --> 00:05:04.780
Born in 1984 in Kansas, Wickersham's midwestern
roots play front and center in her role as

00:05:04.780 --> 00:05:07.110
Ellie Bishop on NCIS.

00:05:07.110 --> 00:05:10.490
Wickersham is in her fourth year with the
show as of the making of this video, and it

00:05:10.490 --> 00:05:12.949
remains her major focus going forward.

00:05:12.949 --> 00:05:18.330
She took a shot at blockbuster fame with roles
in I Am Number Four and 2012's Gone, but the

00:05:18.330 --> 00:05:22.530
mixed reception for those films probably felt
like a big step backwards compared to the

00:05:22.530 --> 00:05:26.939
perpetual success machine that is the NCIS
franchise.

00:05:26.939 --> 00:05:28.860
Sasha Alexander

00:05:28.860 --> 00:05:32.470
By all accounts, Sasha Alexander was born
to be a performer.

00:05:32.470 --> 00:05:37.289
She was acting in school plays by seventh
grade, and on the side she tried out ice skating,

00:05:37.289 --> 00:05:38.379
singing, and dancing.

00:05:38.379 --> 00:05:43.000
These days, she's just about omnipresent on
our TV screens, showing up on a number of

00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:48.849
wildly successful TV shows such as Dawson's
Creek, CSI, Friends, and Shameless, in addition

00:05:48.849 --> 00:05:51.550
to her long-running gig on NCIS.

00:05:51.550 --> 00:05:56.470
It's no shock that this great track record
made her a lock for the 2016's People's Choice

00:05:56.470 --> 00:05:59.720
Award for favorite cable TV actress.

00:05:59.720 --> 00:06:01.389
Joe Spano

00:06:01.389 --> 00:06:07.080
Now over 70 years old, Joe Spano got his start
in the business in 1973 with an appearance

00:06:07.080 --> 00:06:09.909
in George Lucas' classic American Graffiti.

00:06:09.909 --> 00:06:13.789
But his main claim to fame was Hill Street
Blues, on which he played one of the lead

00:06:13.789 --> 00:06:16.470
roles for 144 episodes.

00:06:16.470 --> 00:06:22.160
As FBI special agent Tobias Fornell, Spano
has been weaving in and out of the NCIS narrative

00:06:22.160 --> 00:06:26.760
since the very beginning, appearing whenever
the writers deem it necessary for the FBI

00:06:26.760 --> 00:06:29.449
to poke around in the NCIS' business.

00:06:29.449 --> 00:06:31.740
Cote de Pablo

00:06:31.740 --> 00:06:36.560
Born María José de Pablo Fernández, Cote
de Pablo was born in Chile and lived there

00:06:36.560 --> 00:06:38.840
for ten years before moving to Miami.

00:06:38.840 --> 00:06:43.419
She was hosting her own talk show by age 15,
which should probably make most of us a little

00:06:43.420 --> 00:06:47.380
sad when you think about the typical teenager's
way of passing the time.

00:06:51.460 --> 00:06:53.140
“Good news guys, I spent all my money!”

00:06:53.640 --> 00:06:54.840
“Troy, you can’t bring that in here!”

00:06:55.120 --> 00:06:56.820
“Yes I can, it’s all-terrain, dummy!”

00:06:56.830 --> 00:07:02.310
The actress left her role on NCIS in 2013
for unknown reasons and snagged roles in a

00:07:02.310 --> 00:07:08.310
couple of films, including The 33, a dramatized
recreation of a Chilean mining disaster.

00:07:08.310 --> 00:07:12.410
For now, the world is full of projects for
her choosing, so there's no telling where

00:07:12.410 --> 00:07:13.410
she'll go next.

00:07:13.410 --> 00:07:14.919
Thanks for watching!

00:07:14.919 --> 00:07:17.930
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:07:17.930 --> 00:07:20.360
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love too!

